    {
      "id": "pBMPs1K9WRji2qndgcDXA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 232.1523955343191,
      "y": 2324.061149432546,
      "width": 806,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "at",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1834197085,
      "version": 452,
      "versionNonce": 1020662685,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1782293169586,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "here every Elelments are of type \"Object\" so that it can allow hetrogeneous data.\n\nso,\n\nint n=obj.get(0); // Error\n\nint n= (Integer)obj.get(0); //ok\n\nint s=(String)obj.get(1); //Exception\n\nString s=(String)obj.get(1); //ok\n\n*** Thus Their are two major problem in typeUnsafe \n\n1. EveryTime we need to do Type casting .\n2.  Remembering dataType of every index is very difficult.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "here every Elelments are of type \"Object\" so that it can allow hetrogeneous data.\n\nso,\n\nint n=obj.get(0); // Error\n\nint n= (Integer)obj.get(0); //ok\n\nint s=(String)obj.get(1); //Exception\n\nString s=(String)obj.get(1); //ok\n\n*** Thus Their are two major problem in typeUnsafe \n\n1. EveryTime we need to do Type casting .\n2.  Remembering dataType of every index is very difficult.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
